---
source: crates/qrec-shell/src/doctor.rs
expression: out
---
=== niri
Global shortcuts for niri (paste into ~/.config/niri/config.kdl):

binds {
    Mod+Shift+R { spawn "qrec" "record" "toggle"; }
    Mod+Shift+O { spawn "qrec" "record" "start" "--over-selection"; }
    Mod+Shift+D { spawn "qrec" "take" "discard-last"; }
}

=== sway
Global shortcuts for sway (paste into ~/.config/sway/config):

bindsym $mod+Shift+r exec qrec record toggle
bindsym $mod+Shift+o exec qrec record start --over-selection
bindsym $mod+Shift+d exec qrec take discard-last

=== i3
Global shortcuts for i3 (paste into ~/.config/i3/config):

# i3's default config binds $mod+Shift+r to restart: remove that line.
bindsym $mod+Shift+r exec --no-startup-id qrec record toggle
bindsym $mod+Shift+o exec --no-startup-id qrec record start --over-selection
bindsym $mod+Shift+d exec --no-startup-id qrec take discard-last

=== Hyprland
Global shortcuts for Hyprland (paste into ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.conf):

bind = SUPER SHIFT, R, exec, qrec record toggle
bind = SUPER SHIFT, O, exec, qrec record start --over-selection
bind = SUPER SHIFT, D, exec, qrec take discard-last

=== river
Global shortcuts for river (paste into ~/.config/river/init):

riverctl map normal Super+Shift R spawn 'qrec record toggle'
riverctl map normal Super+Shift O spawn 'qrec record start --over-selection'
riverctl map normal Super+Shift D spawn 'qrec take discard-last'

=== Ubuntu's GNOME
Global shortcuts for GNOME:

In GNOME Settings › Keyboard › View and Customize Shortcuts › Custom Shortcuts,
for each line choose Add Shortcut (or +), type its name and command, then set its shortcut.

Name               Command                             Shortcut
Record toggle      qrec record toggle                  Super+Shift+R
Record over        qrec record start --over-selection  Super+Shift+O
Discard last take  qrec take discard-last              Super+Shift+D

=== KDE Plasma
Global shortcuts for KDE Plasma:

In System Settings › Keyboard › Shortcuts, for each line choose
Add New › Command or Script…, type its command, then set its shortcut.

Name               Command                             Shortcut
Record toggle      qrec record toggle                  Meta+Shift+R
Record over        qrec record start --over-selection  Meta+Shift+O
Discard last take  qrec take discard-last              Meta+Shift+D

=== Xfce
Global shortcuts:

Bind each command to its shortcut in your desktop's keyboard settings.

Name               Command                             Shortcut
Record toggle      qrec record toggle                  Super+Shift+R
Record over        qrec record start --over-selection  Super+Shift+O
Discard last take  qrec take discard-last              Super+Shift+D

